<title>USA: Tremont, Valhi say ruling reversed.</title>
<headline>Tremont, Valhi say ruling reversed.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tremont Corp and Valhi Inc said Wednesday the Delaware Supreme Court has reversed and remanded for further proceedings an earlier ruling favorable to the companies in the case of Kahn vs Tremont Corp et al.</p>
<p>The companies said the suit was originally filed in 1991 following the purchase by Tremont of 7.8 million common shares of NL Industries Inc from Valhi Inc, then the principal stockholder of Tremont. Defendants in the action include Valhi and the members of Tremont's board of directors.</p>
<p>Additional details were not immediately available and spokesmen for the companies were not available to comment.</p>
</text>
